<figcaption>The dummy DAG and its packing (MiB, not measurements). Every step from
<code>metric</code> to <code>nevpt2</code> lies on one path, so all six start at offset 0
and share the bottom 2040 MiB. S, T, V and X are unordered with <code>eri</code>, so
they go above it; S may share with X, which it precedes, and does. The peak equals the
heaviest antichain, so no packing that keeps unordered regions apart does better. From
<code>dag_transitive_closure</code>'s model, in plain Python.</figcaption>
