<figure class="fig" id="budgetfig">
<div class="legend" style="margin:2px 0 6px">
  <span><i class="sw" style="background:var(--c1);border-color:var(--c1)"></i>device</span>
  <span><i class="sw" style="background:var(--c2);border-color:var(--c2)"></i>pinned</span>
  <span><i class="sw" style="background:var(--c3);border-color:var(--c3)"></i>host heap</span>
</div>
<svg id="budgetbars" role="img" aria-label="Each node's mem_budget charge on gly10, by kind, on a log scale from 100 bytes to 10 GB"></svg>
<figcaption>What each node's <code>mem_budget</code> charges on gly10 in cc-pVDZ /
cc-pVDZ-JKFIT (n_ao 734, n_aux 3606, 270,497 pair columns), by kind. Log scale: the
charges span eight decades. Computed from the formulas in the node table, with
the factor, (μν|P) and B one step, <code>eri</code>, and its ERI buffer at an example
<code>mem_per_gpu</code> of 2 GiB. Device charges are per GPU: on every GPU for the metric,
its factor and the ERI buffer, on gpu0 for the rest. The scratch row is the LAPACK formula
for the eigensolve's work at n_ao, not a cuSOLVER query, and the SCF is left out, as in
the graph. The fixed 128 MiB handle workspace is not drawn. Hover a bar for its parts.</figcaption>
</figure>
