</svg>
<figcaption>The same budget as two totals. B is on the host, so the host's cap is the
one a large density-fitted run meets first; a GPU holds its O(N²) data, the ERI buffer and
the handle workspace. Unbatched, with B and the <code>cells</code> work list on gpu0, the
same molecule took 9.86 GB of device memory. The smallest segment is drawn at a minimum
width; its size is in its tooltip.</figcaption>
</figure>
